DESCRIPTION:CHB Lafayette’s Horror Book Club pick for November is You Sho
 uld Have Been Nicer to My Mom by Vincent Tirado.\nWe’ll meet at 6:15 p.m
 . on Nov. 18 at the bookstore to discuss this horror novel!\nPop by the bo
 okshop\, or order your copy here!: https://cavalierhousebooks.com/.../2026
 .../horror-book-club\nSynopsis:\nWhen Papi Ramon\, the patriarch of the we
 althy Abreu family dies\, he gives the family one last message in the will
 : “One of you is el bacà\, the demon that I made a deal with. Get rid o
 f them or you will be damned.” Xiomara\, the uncontested favorite of Pap
 i Ramon (and therefore the least liked in the family)\, watches as everyon
 e dismisses this as the joke of a senile old man and demands the lawyer ob
 tain the previous will Papi wrote.\nWhile the lawyer drives back to his of
 fice\, a storm breaks out\, forcing the entire family—Xiomara’s aunts 
 and uncles and cousins—to remain in the house. And the words of Papi’s
  will hang over their heads even heavier than the rain clouds. Over the co
 urse of the night\, scandal after scandal is revealed to the public about 
 the family. Suddenly a tense few hours of surviving her family turns into 
 a vicious night of recrimination\, violence\, accusations…and murder.\nX
 iomara is faced with an impossible task: uproot a demon and somehow kill i
 t or excise the ghosts that linger within her own family.\nAnd the clock i
 s ticking...\n—---------------------\nHorror Book Club is CHB Lafayette'
 s bimonthly book club focusing on horror and dark stories! A CHB Bookselle
 r leads the discussion\, and we vote at our meetings for our upcoming mont
 hly picks.\n\nhttps://www.downtownlafayette.org/event/horror-book-club-dbd
